{"id":"1b77e4da-abfd-4fb3-b02e-38d4ad70f20f","article_key":"doi:10.1016/j.cell.2026.08.010","title":"Tabula Sapiens 2.0: A comprehensive transcriptomic atlas of human cell types","title_zh":"Tabula Sapiens 2.0：人类细胞类型的全面转录组图谱","doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2026.08.010","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2026.08.010","abstract":"The Tabula Sapiens is a reference human cell atlas containing single-cell transcriptomic data from more than two dozen organs and tissues. Here, we report Tabula Sapiens 2.0, which includes data from nine new donors, doubles the number of cells, and adds four new tissues. These new data include four donors with multiple organs contributed, thus providing a unique dataset in which genetic background, age, and epigenetic effects are controlled for. We illustrate applications of the Tabula Sapiens data in areas as diverse as gene regulation and aging. The Tabula Sapiens contains transcripts from nearly all human transcription factors, thereby providing putative cell-type specificity for nearly every human transcription factor and insights into their potential regulatory roles. We also analyze the transcriptomes of cells expressing canonical genes relating to cellular senescence, revealing the heterogeneity and context-dependent nature of senescence and providing new hypotheses into senescence-associated pathways.","abstract_zh":"Tabula Sapiens 是一份人类细胞参考图谱，包含来自二十余个器官和组织的单细胞转录组数据。本文报告了 Tabula Sapiens 2.0，新增了九位捐献者，细胞数量翻倍，并加入了四种新组织。新数据中有四位捐献者提供了多器官样本，形成了一个独特的数据集，能够在遗传背景、年龄和表观遗传效应得到控制的条件下进行研究。我们展示了 Tabula Sapiens 数据在基因调控、衰老等多领域的应用。该图谱包含几乎所有人类转录因子的转录本，为几乎每一种人类转录因子提供了潜在的细胞类型特异性，并洞察其可能的调控作用。我们还分析了表达与细胞衰老相关的经典基因的细胞转录组，揭示了衰老的异质性和情境依赖性，并提出了关于衰老相关通路的新假设。","snippet":"The Tabula Sapiens is a reference human cell atlas containing single-cell transcriptomic data from more than two dozen organs and tissues. Here, we report Tabula Sapiens 2.0, which includes data from nine new donors, doubles the number of cells, and adds four new tissues. These new data include four d